## 10. Pre-existing defect observed (OUT of scope; recorded, not fixed)

cmd (the `Run diff coverage` step command, as written in validate.yml):
     corepack pnpm test -- --changed --coverage --reporter=json --coverage.reporter=json-summary
exit: 1   (same at base a72b8cc and at fe04ab3)
out:  ERROR  unexpected argument '--changed' found
      > turbo test "--changed" "--coverage" ...
      tip: to pass '--changed' as a value, use '-- --changed'
      ELIFECYCLE  Test failed.

Root cause: the root `test` script is `turbo test`, so `pnpm test -- --changed ...`
forwards `--changed` to turbo, which rejects it. The `Run diff coverage` step
therefore fails before reaching the (now-blocking) threshold step. This predates
this patch set and is not caused by it; it was not part of TEST-P2-002's evidence.
It is left for a separate fix (see PR open questions) because correcting the run
command and reconciling it with the global floors is a different change.

